\h MALACHI
\toc1 Malachi
\toc2 Malachi
\toc3 Mal
\mt2 This book contains the account of Malachi proclaiming that God loves his people, Israel, that he will punish them for their sins, and that later he will restore them. We call this book
\mt1 Malachi
\c 1
\p
\v 1  \add This is\add* the message that Yahweh gave to \add the prophet\add* Malachi to \add give to the people of\add* Israel.
\s1 Yahweh’s love for the people of Israel
\p
\v 2 Yahweh says, “I have \add always\add* loved you \add Israeli people\add*.”
\p
\v 3 But you reply, “In what way have you loved us?”
\p Yahweh replies, “\add This is how I loved you\add*: \add It is true that your ancestor\add* Jacob was [RHQ] Esau’s \add younger\add* brother, and I loved Jacob, but I rejected Esau. I caused his hilly region to become ◄desolate/a place where crops did not grow►. I caused the land which he possessed to become a desert where jackals/wolves live.”
\p
\v 4  \add The descendants of Esau who live in\add* Edom may say, “\add Yes,\add* we have been crushed/ruined, but we will rebuild \add houses\add* in the ruins.”
\p But the Commander of the armies of angels replies, “They may build \add houses again\add*, but I will demolish \add them again\add*. Their \add country\add* will be called ‘The land where wicked people \add live\add*’ and \add their people will be called\add* ‘The people with whom Yahweh is angry forever’.”
\p
\v 5 When you \add Israeli\add* people yourselves see \add what I will do to them\add*, you will say, “\add It is evident far\add* beyond the borders of Israel that Yahweh is \add very\add* great!”
\s1 Unacceptable sacrifices
\p
\v 6 But the Commander of the armies of angels says to the priests, “Boys honor their fathers, and servants \add respect\add* their masters. So, if I am \add like your\add* father and your master, why [RHQ] do you not honor and respect me? You have despised me [MTY]!”
\p But you ask, “◄How/In what way► have we despised you?”
\p
\v 7  \add Yahweh replies,\add* “\add Instead of honoring me, you have despised me\add* by offering sacrifices on my altar that are unacceptable to me.”
\p Then you ask, “What sacrifices have we given that have been unacceptable to you?”
\p \add Yahweh replies,\add* “You think that ◄it does not matter/it is okay► if you do not respect my altar.
\v 8 You offer for sacrifices animals that are blind. ◄Is that not wrong?/That is disgusting!► [RHQ] And you offer for sacrifices animals that are crippled or that have diseases. ◄Is that also not wrong?/That \add also\add* is disgusting!► [RHQ] If you tried to give presents like that to your governor, ◄do you think [RHQ] that he would be pleased?/he would certainly not be pleased!► ◄Would he [RHQ] accept such gifts?He would certainly not accept such gifts!► \add That is what\add* the Commander of the armies of angels says!”
\p
\v 9  \add And he also says,\add* “You plead with me to be merciful to you. But you bring to me sacrifices that are not acceptable to me, so why should I be kind to you [RHQ]?”
\p
\v 10 The Commander of the armies of angels \add also\add* says, “I wish/desire that one of you would shut the gates \add of the temple courtyard\add*, in order that no one could offer those worthless sacrifices. I am not pleased with you, and I will not accept the offerings that you bring to me.
\v 11  \add People of other\add* nations honor me [MTY] \add every day\add*, from sunrise/morning until sunset/evening. All over the world people offer incense and \add other\add* pure/acceptable offerings to me [MTY]. \add They do that\add* because \add people among all\add* the nations know that I [MTY] am \add very\add* great.
\p
\v 12 But you \add priests show that you\add* despise me \add by what you do\add*. You say, ‘\add It is all right if\add* people pollute the altar by bringing sacrifices that are unacceptable.’
\v 13 You say ‘We are tired of \add burning all these sacrifices on the altar\add*.’ You ◄turn up your noses at/act very disrespectfully toward► \add me\add*. When you bring \add to me\add* animals that have been stolen or ones that are crippled or that have diseases, to offer them for sacrifices, \add do you think that\add* [RHQ] I should accept them?
\p
\v 14  \add I will\add* curse anyone who \add tries to\add* cheat \add me\add* by solemnly promising \add to bring to me a perfect\add* ram from his flock \add of sheep\add* and then brings to me one that has defects. \add If anyone does that, I will punish him\add*, because I am a great king; \add I am\add* the Commander of the armies of angels and \add people of the other\add* nations revere me [MTY], \add but you do not\add*!”
\c 2
\s1 A warning to the priests
\p
\v 1 You priests, I will say something to warn you.
\v 2 The Commander of the armies of angels says \add this\add*: “Pay attention \add to what I am saying\add*, and \add then\add* decide [IDM] to honor me [MTY]. If you do not do that, I will curse you, and I will curse \add the things that I have given to you to\add* bless you. And I have already cursed them, because you have not honored [IDM] me.
\v 3 I will punish your descendants [MET], and \add it will be as though\add* I will splatter on your faces \add some of\add* the material inside the stomachs of the animals that are brought to be sacrificed, and you will be thrown away with the rest of that material.
\p
\v 4 When that happens, you will know that I warned you like this, in order that my agreement with \add you priests who are descendants of\add* Levi will continue \add to be obeyed\add*. \add That is what I,\add* the Commander of the armies of angels, am saying \add to you\add*.
\v 5 My agreement with \add your ancestor\add* Levi was because I wanted the priests to live prosperously and peacefully. And that is what I have done for them. I required that they greatly respect me and revere [DOU] me.
\v 6 They told the people that what I instructed them to do was right. And they did not tell [MTY] lies. They worked for me peacefully and loyally, and they helped many people to stop sinning.
\p
\v 7 What priests say [MTY] should enable more people to know \add about me\add*, and people should go to them [MTY] to be taught \add what I want them to know\add*, because priests \add should\add* be messengers from me, the Commander of the armies of angels.
\v 8 But, you priests have stopped doing what I wanted you to do. What you have taught people has caused many \add of them\add* to sin. You have rejected the agreement \add that I made\add* with \add the descendants of\add* Levi \add long ago\add*.
\v 9 Therefore I have caused all the people to despise you, and I have caused you to be humiliated, because you have not obeyed me. When you teach \add people\add* my commands, you do not treat all \add people\add* equally.”
\s1 Wrong things that they have done regarding marriage
\p
\v 10  \add Now I will warn you about something else\add*. We all certainly [RHQ] have the same \add heavenly\add* Father. We are certainly [RHQ] \add all\add* created by the same God. So why are [RHQ] \add some of\add* you disobeying/despising the agreement \add that Yahweh made\add* with our ancestors, by not doing for each other what you said that you would do?
\p
\v 11  \add You people of\add* Judah have been unfaithful \add to Yahweh\add*. You have done detestable things in Jerusalem and in \add other places\add* in Israel. You Israeli men have defiled the temple that Yahweh loves. \add You have done that by\add* marrying women who worship idols.
\v 12 I wish that Yahweh would expel from Israel every man who has done that, \add even though\add* they \add say that they are obeying\add* the Commander of the armies of angels by bringing offerings to him.
\p
\v 13 This is another thing that you do: You cover Yahweh’s altar with your tears. You wail because he no longer pays attention to your offerings; but he is not pleased with them.
\v 14 You \add cry out\add*, saying, “Why does Yahweh not like our offerings?” The answer is that Yahweh heard what each of you men solemnly promised to your wives when you were young. But you men have not done what you promised your wives; you sent them away, the ones to whom you made that agreement.
\p
\v 15 It is certainly [RHQ] Yahweh who joined you together. Your spirits and your bodies belong to him. \add So\add* what he wants [RHQ] from you are godly children. So make sure that each of you men remain ◄with/loyal to► the woman that you married when you were young.
\p
\v 16 Yahweh, the God to whom \add we\add* Israelis belong, says, “I hate divorce!” \add So\add* if you men divorce your wives, you are overwhelming them by being cruel to them. So be sure that you are ◄not disloyal/remain united► to your wives. \add That is what\add* the Commander of the armies of angels says.
\p
\v 17 Yahweh \add also says\add*, “What you have said has caused me to become disgusted.”
\p You reply, “What have we said that caused him to become disgusted?”
\p \add The answer is that you have caused him to become disgusted\add* by saying that Yahweh is pleased with all those who do evil things. \add You have caused him to become disgusted\add* by \add constantly\add* asking, “Why does God not act fairly?”
\c 3
\s1 The time of judgment is near
\p
\v 1 The Commander of the armies of angels says \add this\add*: “Listen! I \add am about to\add* send my messenger who will prepare \add the people to receive me\add* when I come. \add You claim that\add* [IRO] you are wanting to see me, and I will suddenly come to my temple. The messenger \add who will tell you about a new\add* agreement, the one whom you are eagerly [SAR] awaiting, is certainly going to come \add to you\add*.”
\p
\v 2 But will anyone [RHQ] be able to survive when he comes? Will anyone [RHQ] be able to \add remain\add* standing in front of him? \add Certainly not,\add* because he will be like [SIM] a blazing fire that refines/purifies \add metal/gold\add*. He will be like [SIM] a very strong soap \add that bleaches clothes\add*.
\v 3  \add He will be like a worker who\add* sits \add in front of his work\add* to cause silver to become pure by burning all the impurities. Like \add a worker refines\add* silver and gold, he will cause the ◄descendants of Levi/priests► to become pure, \add in order that they will again become acceptable to\add* offer sacrifices that will be acceptable to him.
\v 4 When that happens, Yahweh will \add again\add* accept the offerings brought to him by \add the people of\add* Jerusalem and \add other places in\add* Judah, as \add he did\add* previously.
\p
\v 5  \add This is what\add* the Commander of the armies of angels says: “At that time, I will come to you to judge you. I will quickly testify against \add all\add* those who practice sorcery/witchcraft, \add all \add*those who have committed adultery, and \add all\add* liars. \add I will testify\add* against those who have not given their workers the pay/wages that they promised, those who ◄oppress/treat cruelly► widows and orphans, and those who do not allow foreigners who live among you to be treated fairly. \add I will testify that all\add* the people who do those things do not revere me.”
\s1 Not bringing tithes
\p
\v 6 “I am Yahweh, and I never change. And although you \add deceive people like\add* your ancestor Jacob did, I have not \add yet\add* gotten rid of you.
\v 7 You and your ancestors have ignored my commands and you have not obeyed them. \add Now\add* return to me; and when that happens, I will ◄return/do good► to you. \add That is what I,\add* the Commander of the armies of angels, say.”
\p But you ask, “\add We have never gone away from you, so\add* how can we return \add to you\add*?”
\p
\v 8  \add I reply,\add* “People should certainly not [RHQ] cheat God; but you people have cheated me!”
\p You ask, “In what way did we cheat you?”
\p \add I reply,\add* “\add You have cheated me by not bringing to me each year\add* ◄the tithes/one tenth of \add all\add* your crops and animals► and \add other\add* offerings \add that you are required to give to me\add*.
\v 9 All that you do is cursed, because all you people in this country have been cheating me.
\v 10  \add Now\add* bring all the tithes to the storage rooms \add in the temple\add*, in order that there will be \add enough\add* food \add for the people who serve me\add* there. If you do that, I, the Commander of the armies of angels, promise that I will open the windows of heaven, and pour out \add from them\add* blessings on you. \add If you bring your tithes to the temple, the blessings will be\add* very great, with the result that you will not have enough space to store all of them. So test me \add to see if I am telling the truth\add*.
\v 11 You will have abundant crops \add to harvest\add*, because I will protect them in order that they will not be harmed by locusts/insects. Your grapes will not fall from the vines \add before they are ripe\add*.
\v 12 When that happens, \add the people of\add* all nations will say that \add I\add* have blessed you, because your country will be delightful. \add That is what I,\add* the Commander of the armies of angels, say.
\b
\p
\v 13  \add I,\add* Yahweh, \add have something else\add* to say \add to you\add*. You have said terrible things about me.”
\p But you reply, “What terrible things have we said about you?”
\p
\v 14  \add I reply\add*, “You have said, ‘It is useless \add for us\add* to serve God. We have gained nothing [RHQ] by obeying the commands that he gave \add to us\add* and by trying to show the Commander of the armies of angels that we are sorry \add for the sins that we have committed\add*.
\v 15 From now on, we will say/consider that those who are proud are \add the ones whom God has\add* blessed. \add We will say that because it seems that it is\add* those who do evil who become rich, and \add that it is\add* those who try to find out how many evil things they can do without God punishing them who are not punished.’”
\p
\v 16 After \add the people heard my message\add*, those who revered Yahweh discussed \add those things\add* with each other, and Yahweh listened to what they said. While Yahweh was watching, they wrote on a scroll the things that would remind them \add about what they promised\add*, and they wrote on that scroll the names of those who revered Yahweh and who \add said that they\add* always wanted to honor him [MTY].
\p
\v 17 The Commander of the armies of angels says this \add about those people\add*: “They will be my people. At the time that I judge people, \add they will be like\add* [MET] a special treasure to me. I will be kind to them, like [SIM] fathers are kind to their sons who obey them.
\v 18 When that happens, you will again see that \add the manner in which I treat\add* righteous people is different from \add the manner in which I treat\add* wicked people. \add You will see that the manner in which I act toward\add* those who serve me is different from \add the manner in which I act toward\add* those who do not.”
\c 4
\s1 The coming time of punishment
\p
\v 1  \add This is also what\add* the Commander of the armies of angels says: “There will be a time that I will judge \add and punish\add* people. \add When that happens, it will be\add* like [SIM] a very hot furnace. At that time, all the proud and wicked people will be burned up like [MET] stubble burns. They will be burned up completely, \add like\add* roots and branches \add and everything else on a tree burns completely in a very hot fire\add*.
\v 2 But \add as for\add* you who revere me [MTY], \add the one who will save you will come to you\add* like [MET] \add the sun shines in the morning, and enable you to\add* become righteous (OR, \add do what is\add* righteous); he will restore you \add and protect you like a bird protects its chicks\add* [MET] under its wings. \add When he comes,\add* you will \add be very joyful\add*, like [SIM] calves that go out from a barn into the pasture leaping \add joyfully\add*.
\v 3 At the time when I judge people, you will tread on wicked people as though [SIM] they were the dirt under your feet. \add That is what I\add*, the Commander of the armies of angels, promise.
\p
\v 4 Be sure to obey the laws that I gave to Moses, who served me \add well\add*. \add Obey all\add* the commandments and regulations that I gave him on Sinai \add Mountain\add*, for all \add you people of\add* Israel \add to obey.\add*
\p
\v 5 Listen \add to this: Some day\add* I will send to you the prophet Elijah. \add He will arrive\add* before the great and dreadful/terrible day when \add I\add*, Yahweh, \add will judge and punish people\add*.
\v 6 Because of what he \add preaches\add*, parents and their children will \add love\add* each other \add again\add* [IDM]. If that does not happen, I will come and curse your country \add and destroy it\add*.”
